# The descriptor is one record that a constant holds: its `value` is stored anew before each call and emptied behind it. The built-in reads `value` off it: all that the flow holds in that field lies under the name, never "the last store". Descriptor and object stay in sight. L0 = what is laid, L1 = the object, L2 = the descriptor.
# RUN: link fields mechanisms=all
# CHECK: field L0.2 "run" appended proven=f2 writers-known
# CHECK: field L1.0 "inner" proven=undefined|L0 writers-known
# CHECK: field L2.1 "value" proven=undefined|L0 writers-known
